<title>LITHUANIA: YIELDS ON 91-DAY T-BILLS EDGE UP A BIT.</title>
<headline>YIELDS ON 91-DAY T-BILLS EDGE UP A BIT.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields edged up a bit on 91-day</p>
<p>Lithuanian Treasury bills at Monday's auction and all of the 50</p>
<p>million litas issue was sold, the country's central bank said.</p>
<p>The average yield was 9.19 percent, up a wisp from the 9.18</p>
<p>percent offered to buyers at the last auction for 91-day paper</p>
<p>on May 5.</p>
<p>The settlement date is May 15 and the bills mature on</p>
<p>August 14.</p>
<p>All figures in millions of litas unless otherwise</p>
<p>indicated.</p>
<p>SOLD  DEMAND  MIN/MAX YIELD  AV. YIELD  LAST AV. YIELD</p>
<p>50    71.888    8.90/9.45	 9.19	  9.18</p>
<p>-- Ed Stoddard, Riga newsroom +371 21 52 40</p>
